{{NZelectorateShortDesc|type=general|current=yes|region=wellington}}
'''Hutt South''' is a parliamentary [[New Zealand electorates|electorate]] in the lower [[Hutt Valley]] and the [[Wellington]] suburb of [[Newlands, Wellington|Newlands]] of New Zealand. It is held by [[Chris Bishop]] of the [[New Zealand National Party|National Party]] following the {{NZ election link|2023}}. It was previously held by [[Ginny Andersen]] of the [[New Zealand Labour Party|Labour Party]] from 2020 to 2023.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/82433937/labour-mp-trevor-mallard-vacates-hutt-south-electorate-to-apply-for-speaker-position |title=Labour MP Trevor Mallard vacates Hutt South electorate to apply for Speaker position |first=Nicholas |last=Boyack |publisher=Stuff.co.nz |date=25 July 2016 |access-date=25 July 2016}}</ref>

==Population centres==
The electorate is based on the southern part of the city of [[Lower Hutt]]. It was formed in 1996 from the [[Pencarrow (electorate)|Pencarrow]] and [[Eastern Hutt]] electorates, which were abolished. Hutt South consists of the southern suburbs of Lower Hutt, [[Petone]], [[Wainuiomata]], and [[Eastbourne, New Zealand|Eastbourne]].<ref name="Electorate Profile">{{cite web |title=Electorate Profile Hutt South|url= http://www.parliament.nz/NR/rdonlyres/A1075329-135E-4698-B5E8-2B2B0BB0E85E/124/Hutt_South1.pdf |publisher=Parliamentary Library|access-date=29 November 2011|format=PDF|date=October 2005}}</ref>

=== 2014 boundary review ===
{{maplink|from=New Zealand Electorates/2020/General/Hutt South.map|frame-longitude=174.92|frame-latitude=-41.28|zoom=9|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries at the [[2020 New Zealand general election|2020]] and [[2023 New Zealand general election|2023]] general elections)}}
Following the 2014 boundary review, Hutt South lost [[Naenae]] and a small part of [[Epuni]] to {{NZ electorate link|Rimutaka}}<!-- do not change to the current spelling as this is how it was spelled in 2014 -->, in exchange for the suburbs of [[Kelson, New Zealand|Kelson]] and [[Belmont, Wellington|Belmont]]. It also gained the suburbs of [[Tirohanga]], [[Harbour View, New Zealand|Harbour View]], [[Normandale, New Zealand|Normandale]], [[Maungaraki]] and [[Korokoro, New Zealand|Korokoro]] from {{NZ electorate link|Ōhariu}}, meaning the entire Hutt Valley was now covered by just two electorates (Rimutaka and Hutt South).

Since 2014, the following suburbs of Lower Hutt fall within Hutt South.<ref>{{cite web |url= http://www.huttcity.govt.nz/Documents/maps/HuttCityWardsSuburbs.pdf |title= Hutt City Wards and Suburbs |publisher= Hutt City Council |access-date= 17 September 2013 |url-status= dead |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20130209145201/http://huttcity.govt.nz/Documents/maps/HuttCityWardsSuburbs.pdf |archive-date= 9 February 2013 }}</ref>
