=== 2025 boundary review ===
In the 2025 boundary review, Hutt South and Remutaka both shifted south-westwards, with the former taking in [[Newlands, Wellington|Newlands]], a suburb of [[Wellington|Wellington City]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |url=https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/historical-events/boundary-review-2025/report-of-the-representation-commission-2025/ |access-date=2025-08-15 |website=Elections |language=en-NZ}}</ref> This is effective from the 2026 election.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Timetable |url=https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/historical-events/boundary-review-2025/timetable/ |access-date=2025-08-15 |website=Elections |language=en-NZ}}</ref>

==History==
At the first [[Mixed-member proportional representation|MMP]] election in {{NZ election link year|1996}}, Hutt South replaced the earlier electorate of [[Pencarrow (New Zealand electorate)|Pencarrow]], which was then held by [[Trevor Mallard]]. Mallard was returned at every general election until he moved to list-only at the 2017 election.<ref name="Mallard parliamentary bio">{{cite web|title=Hon Trevor Mallard|url= http://www.parliament.nz/en-NZ/MPP/MPs/MPs/c/c/b/50MP1551-Mallard-Trevor.htm |publisher=New Zealand Parliament|access-date=29 November 2011}}</ref>

